        ]
      },
      {
        "finding": "A zero-shot CoT suffix lowers HPR on all models under FICDETAIL (Figure 3). Most DCCH/RCH comparisons say outputs with CoT are more harmful and detailed (Figure 4). No numbers are given in the text.",
        "proposed_claim": "CoT prompting lowers jailbreak compliance but raises the detail and harmfulness of the responses that do comply.",
        "row_ids": [
          "r10",
          "r11"
        ]
      },
      {
        "finding": "Reasoning models' jailbroken outputs are usually judged more harmful and specific than those of their non-reasoning counterparts: DCCH 1.01–1.73, except 0.77 for QwQ vs Qwen32B with the Llama judge. RCH is 0.54 for DS-R1 vs DS-V3.",
        "proposed_claim": "Jailbroken reasoning models give more detailed and actionable harmful content than non-reasoning models; the size of the gap depends on the judge and the model pair.",
